    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n30564" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">nāvĭger</span></b> ,
			ĕra, ĕrum, adj.
		navis-gero. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Ship-bearing, navigable</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">mare navigerum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Lucr. 1,
					3</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">iter,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Mart. 12, 99, 4</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Sailing</i>: navigera similitudo, <i>the likeness of a vessel under sail;</i> said of a sea-mussel,
				<i><span class="en">Plin.
				9, 30, 49, § 94</span></i>; v. nauplius.</div>
